From: gstreamer-custom-build local patches
Subject: [PATCH] h264decoder: do not dereference a released second-field frame

gst_h264_decoder_finish_current_picture() releases the current
GstVideoCodecFrame when the subclass' end_picture() fails, and then still
calls gst_h264_decoder_finish_picture() for the picture (now marked
non-existing).

If that picture is the second field of a pair whose first field belongs to a
different codec frame, finish_picture() looks both frames up again with
gst_video_decoder_get_frame(). The second field's frame was just released, so
the lookup returns NULL, but only first_field is checked:

    if (first_field) {
      if (GST_CLOCK_TIME_IS_VALID (first_field->pts) &&
          GST_CLOCK_TIME_IS_VALID (second_field->pts)) {   <- NULL->pts

and the process dies with an access violation reading address 0x20 (the
offset of GstVideoCodecFrame::pts). gst_video_decoder_release_frame() at the
end of the block would also be called with NULL.

end_picture() fails for example when

  a) d3d11/dxva decoders receive FLUSH_START while the streaming thread is
     between new_picture() and end_picture(): gst_d3d11_decoder_begin_frame()
     returns GST_FLOW_FLUSHING, which happens on every pipeline teardown that
     flushes the decoder first, and
  b) a field arrives without decodable slice data ("No bitstream buffer to
     submit"), which live interlaced (PAFF) streams over RTP/UDP hit after
     packet loss.

Observed with d3d11h264dec on 1080i H.264 RTP multicast streams: the display
process crashed in gst_h264_decoder_finish_picture() (gsth264decoder.c, the
second_field->pts check) on the queue's streaming thread while another thread
was sending FLUSH_START to the decoder.

Skip the duration update and the release when the second field's frame is
already gone. Upstream main has the same code.

--- a/_p2_/gst-libs/gst/codecs/gsth264decoder.c
+++ b/_p2_/gst-libs/gst/codecs/gsth264decoder.c
@@ -2284,9 +2284,12 @@
 
     /* Update frame duration. since we output a frame for two input field
      * pictures, output buffer duration should be first-field-duration +
-     * second-field-duration */
+     * second-field-duration.
+     * second_field is NULL when its codec frame was already released, e.g.
+     * by gst_h264_decoder_finish_current_picture() after end_picture()
+     * failed (flushing, or a field without decodable slices) */
     if (first_field) {
-      if (GST_CLOCK_TIME_IS_VALID (first_field->pts) &&
+      if (second_field && GST_CLOCK_TIME_IS_VALID (first_field->pts) &&
           GST_CLOCK_TIME_IS_VALID (second_field->pts)) {
         GstClockTime first_field_end_time = first_field->pts;
         GstClockTime frame_end_time = second_field->pts;
@@ -2316,7 +2319,8 @@
           GST_CODEC_PICTURE_FRAME_NUMBER (picture->other_field));
     }
 
-    gst_video_decoder_release_frame (decoder, second_field);
+    if (second_field)
+      gst_video_decoder_release_frame (decoder, second_field);
   }
 
   /* C.4.4 */
